From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: crackerjacques <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rg-ds: make OTG-C port dual-role so USB
 hubs work

The mainline rk3568-anbernic-rg-ds DTS pins the type-C OTG controller to
dr_mode = "peripheral" so the ttyGS0 gadget console is guaranteed. The side
effect is that the OTG-C port can never enter host mode: plugging in a USB
hub (or any downstream device) does nothing, because the controller stays a
gadget and no VBUS is driven.

Switch the port to dr_mode = "otg" (the same dual-role approach used on the
Anbernic RG Vita Pro and the mainline Powkiddy X55). When the port is idle or
tethered to a host PC it still enumerates as a gadget, so the g_serial ttyGS0
console keeps working; when a downstream device/hub is attached the rockchip
usb2phy ID/VBUS detection flips it to host mode.

VBUS for the port comes from the rk817 boost through the OTG_SWITCH
regulator. It must not be tied to the PHY as phy-supply: the PHY is powered
whenever dwc3 is up, so the boost would be on permanently, and while it is
on the rk817 measures its own boost as charger input and ignores a real
charger plugged into the DC port. Instead, hand OTG_SWITCH to a
regulator-output node: VBUS stays off at boot so the battery charges, and
userspace switches it on through the node's "state" attribute when a
bus-powered device needs power.

Signed-off-by: crackerjacques <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
---
 .../dts/rockchip/rk3568-anbernic-rg-ds.dts    | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-anbernic-rg-ds.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-anbernic-rg-ds.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-anbernic-rg-ds.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-anbernic-rg-ds.dts
@@ -313,6 +313,16 @@
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * 5V VBUS on the OTG-C port comes from the rk817 boost through OTG_SWITCH.
+	 * While it is on, the rk817 sees its own boost as charger input and ignores
+	 * a real charger, so keep it off and let userspace switch it on on demand.
+	 */
+	otg_vbus: otg-vbus {
+		compatible = "regulator-output";
+		vout-supply = <&otg_switch>;
+	};
+
 	leds: pwm-leds {
 		compatible = "pwm-leds";
 
@@ -1217,7 +1227,7 @@
 };
 
 &usb_host0_xhci {
-	dr_mode = "peripheral";
+	dr_mode = "otg";
 	phy-names = "usb2-phy";
 	phys = <&usb2phy0_otg>;
 	maximum-speed = "high-speed";
-- 
Armbian

